<h1>Sustainability</h1>

<p>Foundry operations use a significant amount of energy and raw material, and Meridian Castings has run a group-wide programme since 2023 to reduce both. The programme is overseen by the Chief Operating Officer and reported to the board twice a year.</p>

<p>At Sheffield, waste heat recovered from the melting furnaces now pre-heats combustion air, reducing gas use per tonne cast. At all three sites, used moulding sand is reclaimed and reused wherever the casting specification allows, cutting both landfill volume and the amount of new sand purchased each year. Wrexham and Poznan have replaced older lighting and compressed air systems with more efficient equipment as part of routine plant upgrades.</p>

<p>Our current target is a group-wide reduction in energy use per tonne cast, measured against a 2022 baseline, to be reviewed at the end of 2027. Progress is reported alongside our other quality and operational metrics; see <a href="/quality">quality management</a> for how these are tracked, or read about specific site upgrades in our <a href="/newsroom">newsroom</a>.</p>
